  "notes": "Per the 2026-2027 Texas A&M University undergraduate catalog: Kinesiology — Strength and Conditioning Track (BS). Prerequisites are not listed in the catalog's plan of study grid; consult course descriptions.\nCatalog footnotes:\n[grid1 fn1] Must make a grade of C or better.\n[grid1 fn2] MATH 148 , MATH 152 , MATH 168 , or MATH 172 will be accepted in lieu of MATH 140 .\n[grid1 fn3] Must take KINE 199 Majors Sport Conditioning. Participation in band or athletics cannot be used for KINE 199 credit. KINE 199 activities cannot be repeated for credit and must be taken for a grade. Must have HKAE attribute.\n[grid1 fn4] Must be taken at Texas A&M University.\n[grid1 fn5] MATH 147 , MATH 151 , or MATH 171 will be accepted in lieu of MATH 142 .\n[grid1 fn6] Course selection should meet the International and Cultural Diversity (ICD) or the Cultural Discourse (CD) graduation requirement, if needed.\n[grid1 fn7] Must be chosen from the following courses and in consultation with your advisor BIOL 112 , BIOL 206 ; CHEM 119 , CHEM 120 ; KINE 216/HLTH 216 , KINE 325/CTSE 325 , KINE 485 , KINE 491 ; NUTR 222 , NUTR 300-499; PBSI 300-499; PHLT 354/HLTH 354 ; PHYS 202 ; STAT 201 , or STAT 301 , or STAT 302 , or STAT 303 ; SOCI 205 ; SPMT 304 .\n[grid1 fn8] Meets the graduation requirement for writing",
